From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P4R4D16M4 <patrickheinzelbecker@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:59:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] mtd: comcerto-nand: register the stock kernel2 partition read-only

The stock firmware boots from kernel1 or kernel2; the UntrashOS loader
goes into the other one.  untrash-pfe-firmware reads the PE firmware
from the stock slot recorded at install time (ACTIVE_SLOT), so both
kernel partitions must be readable.  Appended after kernel1 to keep the
mtd numbers; the parent MTD stays non-writable.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/comcerto-nand.c
@@ -130,6 +130,15 @@ static const struct mtd_partition comcerto_nand_v213_parts[] = {
 		.offset = 10 * 1024 * 1024,
 		.size = 10 * 1024 * 1024,
 	},
+	/*
+	 * The other stock kernel slot (after rootfs1); which of the two holds
+	 * the stock kernel is ACTIVE_SLOT of the install run.  Read-only.
+	 */
+	{
+		.name = "kernel2",
+		.offset = 130 * 1024 * 1024,
+		.size = 10 * 1024 * 1024,
+	},
 };
 
 static inline struct comcerto_nand *to_comcerto_nand(struct nand_chip *chip)
